        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe design is otherwise well-aligned with the codebase: putting the age-band computation on the `Owner` domain entity (`getAgeBand()`) sits naturally alongside the existing derived getters `getMembershipLevel()`, `getCheckDigit()`, and `getIdentityKey()`, and the `@AfterMapping addAgeBand` follows the exact pattern of its siblings (`addCheckDigit`, `addMembershipLevel`, `addLocality`). The schema and OpenAPI additions are purely additive and consistent. No duplication and no catch-all creep.\n\nOne concrete, actionable structural/idiom nit:\n\n- `Owner.java:150` uses the fully-qualified `java.time.Period.between(...)` inline, even though the file already imports from the same package (`import java.time.LocalDate;` at line 25). This is inconsistent with the file's own import style. Add `import java.time.Period;` and use the short name `Period.between(...)` so it reads like the rest of the file.\n\nThat's the only change needed; the rest of the structure is fine as-is."
